  "notes": [
    "Reset: the vault proxy ran VaultPinkBNB from creation; its wiring followed within 150 blocks: setRewardsToken (slot 0x167), setMinter (slot 0xcf, with the minter's setMinter grant two blocks earlier) and setPinkChef (slot 0xd0), which getReward also calls, so the last of these sets the age. The later slot 0x168/0x169 writes are notifyRewardAmount's reward schedule.",
    "Campaign: every transaction minting over 3,000 PINK (Etherscan PINK mints, normal mints were at most 1,708 before) until PINK's price fell: 30 calls by 0xdfd78a97 through 0x33f9bb37 and 15 by 0xce1f4b4f through 0xc31d7f2c, both cashing out through Tornado. Two large mints in the same window by a withdrawAll (0x2622516c) and another vault's getReward (0xc936e641) are users sweeping leftover donated CAKE and are not counted. The attacker's earlier contracts (0xefc5ac41, 0x5538d3de, 0x42b15779) and its own getReward 0x14516e37 minted no excess PINK.",
    "Loss is the PINK/WBNB pair 0x711de3b5's WBNB depletion in the campaign and in 0xdfd78a97's four router sales of the minted PINK (refs), the attackers' realised value (rule 12): 3,110.7 BNB, close to the 2,890 BNB the two attacker EOAs sent to Tornado. ImmuneBytes' 429k USD figure appears to cover only part of it."
